OL,3,GNEWSASheku Bayoh Inquiry publishes     
OL,4,Aclosing submissions                    
OL,6,FThe public inquiry into the death of   
OL,7,FSheku Bayoh has published closing      
OL,8,Fsubmissions from key participants.     
OL,10,FBayoh, a father-of-two, died aged 31 in
OL,11,FMay 2015 after being restrained by six 
OL,12,Fpolice officers on a street in         
OL,13,FKirkcaldy, Fife.                       
OL,15,FThe public inquiry, launched in 2020,  
OL,16,Fhas been examining what happened       
OL,17,Fbefore, during and after his death and 
OL,18,Fwhether race was a factor.             
OL,20,FInquiry chair Lord Colbeck is          
OL,21,Fconsidering the evidence before        
OL,22,Fdelivering a final report.             
